.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt SCRSHOT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm scrshot
.Nd save the PicoCalc panel to an image file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl f Ar ppm | bmp | raw
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the controller memory behind the 320 by 320 panel through
.Pa /dev/lcdgfx
and writes it to
.Ar file
one row at a time.
It needs the superuser, because the memory holds the text console's screen
from before the open, and a PICOCALC_SD kernel, the one built with
.Dv LCD_GFX_EXT .
.Pp
Opening the device takes the panel from the text console but leaves the
memory as the console drew it, and the console keeps its cell store current
meanwhile, so the capture shows the screen as it stood when
.Nm
started.
The console scrolls by moving the controller's scroll start, so the glass
shows memory line
.Pq T + y
mod 320 at screen row y.
.Nm
asks the kernel for T with
.Dv LCDG_XINFO ,
which reports the memory line the console showed at the top of the glass
when it gave up the panel, and reads the lines in that order, so the image
matches the glass from top to bottom.
When the panel is closed again the console repaints its text.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-f format"
.It Fl a
Save all 480 lines of controller memory in memory order, 320 by 480
pixels, instead of the visible window.
Lines 320 to 479 lie below the visible area and hold whatever a pixel
program drew there.
.It Fl f Ar format
.Cm ppm ,
the default, is a binary PPM (P6) with 8 bits per channel.
.Cm bmp
is a 24-bit BMP, stored top down, with each row padded to four bytes.
.Cm raw
is the RGB565 rows as the kernel returned them, two bytes per pixel, low
byte first, with no header.
.It Fl o Ar file
The output file.
The default is
.Pa /tmp/scrshot.ppm ,
or the same name with the extension of the chosen format.
.El
.Pp
The controller returns six bits per component and the kernel keeps the
upper five, six and five of red, green and blue, which
.Nm
widens to eight bits by bit replication.
Only a few rows are in memory at a time.
A failed read or write ends the run with a message that names the row, and
the partial file is removed.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/lcdgfx" -compact
.It Pa /dev/lcdgfx
the panel's pixel device
.It Pa /tmp/scrshot.ppm
the default output
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the file is complete, 1 on any failure and 2 on a usage error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr paneltest 1
.Sh CAVEATS
Only one program can hold
.Pa /dev/lcdgfx ,
so
.Nm
fails with a busy device while a pixel program runs.
